    "title": "Hydraulic press — Pascal's principle in pencil",
    "description": "Two pistons of unequal area connected by an incompressible fluid. Push down with force F on the small piston; the large piston pushes up with force F × (A_big / A_small). Pascal, 1647. Why a single foot can lift a car.",
